SimpleTuner CuTe attention

Kernel implementation synchronized with KohakuFA-CuTe 0.4.0 revision
c373d7bf0a7096a9be0fcc7e488191414aac959c.
https://github.com/SimpleTuner-io/KohakuFA-CuTe

The implementation is distributed under AGPL-3.0-or-later;
see LICENSE.AGPL-3.0. SimpleTuner retains its training backend policy,
package namespaces and public attention adapters.

Explicit 2D neighborhood attention supports shifted boundary windows without
a NATTEN dependency. It uses normalized dQ and reconstructed dK corrections
by default, with bounded H100 scheduling and owned-gradient spatial traversal.

Supported CuTe architectures are SM80, SM86, SM89, SM90, SM100, SM103,
SM120 and SM121. The default arithmetic preserves unscaled score maxima,
separate logarithmic normalization, one input-dtype conversion of P and dS,
FP32 product accumulation and late dQ/dK scaling. Backward uses the actual
rounded forward output for its output/dO correction. Compensated precision
helpers remain explicit experiments, outside default dispatch.

The optional FA4-derived schedules retain their pinned runtime and source
eligibility checks. Atomic backward follows the live deterministic policy;
owned-gradient kernels retain their independent reduction semantics.
Native caches include the C++ source hash, and logical negative/conjugate
view values are resolved before the DLPack boundary.

